      ],
      "definition": "Counter-argument comments (OC_comments): any comment introduces a concrete, external factual analogy",
      "kind": "prompt",
      "spec": "Read the OC_comments JSON list (comments by users other than the OP). Return 1 if at least one comment introduces a concrete analogy drawn from outside the OP's own scenario, based on a specific real-world case, event, fact or situation (e.g. a named or specific historical, scientific, legal or everyday case) used as a comparison to the issue being argued. Purely abstract reasoning, hypotheticals with no real-world factual basis, and mere restatement of the OP's own examples do not count. Return 0 if the list is valid and no comment does so. Return null if OC_comments is missing or malformed. Empty list gives 0. Use only OC_comments; do not use conversation or later replies."
